 "theorem": "Conditional on the Stage E theorem of results/fourier-existence-N32.json (a real rotating wave x_j(t) = phi(omega t + 2 pi j / N) of the ring of N = 32 cells (c = N^2 / 64000 per ms), period T = 2 pi / omega; status: awaiting adversarial review) and on the lemmas of fourier/LEMMAS-stability.md: with delta = 0.000005000000000000663635812970 per ms (exact dyadic, recorded), every eigenvalue mu of the Hill operator H_0 with Re mu >= -delta lies in i omega N Z and is algebraically simple (Theorem 3). Hence (Theorem 4): the monodromy Y(T) has the Floquet multiplier 1 algebraically simple, and all other 575 Floquet multipliers have modulus < e^(-delta T) <= 0.9997320954221904942011761; the shift-reduced map M_tau = Q^(-1) Y(tau), tau = T / N, has the eigenvalue 1 algebraically simple and all other eigenvalues of modulus < e^(-delta tau) <= 0.9999916268953467731405854 (so does the derivative of every section map of Corollary 1.3, without the eigenvalue 1: spectral radius < 0.9999916268953467731405854); the orbit is locally exponentially orbitally stable with asymptotic phase.",
